# Binary formats git's NUL-byte heuristic can misread as text. A vector
# PDF built from plain-text object streams has no NUL in its first block,
# so without this rule diff/apply run CRLF normalisation over it and
# corrupt the byte-exact fixture (seen live on grundriss_erdgeschoss.pdf).
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.docx binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary

# ABS rebar schedules (BVBS) terminate records with CRLF and checksum
# every character, so a line-ending conversion would break the sample.
*.abs -text
